**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** The closed sets a version row stores get their disk tags, and a sample's material references keep their versions (001 §C 'Hybrid shape': lifecycle, protection, pin and the sample-version → material-version keys are relational columns; AGENTS.md: a closed set's disk tag is a 1-based `int`, read back by `tryOfDb`). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Lifecycle.fs`: `EntryLifecycle` (`:31-33`) gains `member this.value : int` (`ActiveEntry` 1, `InactiveEntry` 2) and `static member tryOfDb (v : int) : EntryLifecycle option`, which answers `None` for any other tag. Directly after it, new `PinState` = `VersionPinned` | `VersionUnpinned`, with `value` (1, 2) and `tryOfDb` the same way. Its doc is one to three lines: whether a library version is pinned; a pin is one-way, set when a kit first references the version or when it is exported, and a pinned version never mutates (001 §C 'Pinned replaces VersionsInUse'; spec 0050). This step adds the type only: `VersionsInUse` and every store are unchanged. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs`: `EntryProtection` (`ElementId.fs:EntryProtection`) gains `value` (`ProtectedBuiltIn` 1, `UserManaged` 2) and `tryOfDb` the same way. `SampleStructure` gains `member this.referencedMaterialVersions : Set<MaterialVersionId>`: every material version the structure references (each film layer, a `Repeated` group's cell counted once; the substrate plate; the lower half-space), each kept at its own version. `referencedMaterials` (`ElementId.fs:SampleStructure.referencedMaterials`) becomes that set projected to `materialId`, so the structure is walked in one place; its doc says so in no more words. Each new member's doc is one line citing spec 0050. No other type, member or caller changes. (3) Tests. `LifecycleTests` gains `lifecycle, protection and pin states round-trip their database tags`: each of the six cases answers its tag above, `tryOfDb` of each tag answers its case, and `tryOfDb` of 0 and of 3 answers `None` for all three sets. `MaterialProxyTests` gains `referencedMaterialVersions keeps every referenced material version, a repeated cell once`: `(BuiltinCatalogue.sample SampleIds.multilayerQwId).structure.referencedMaterialVersions` is exactly `MaterialVersionId.firstOf` of `MaterialIds.glass152` and `MaterialIds.vacuumMaterial`; `SampleIds.langasiteSiliconId`'s is exactly `firstOf` of `MaterialIds.langasite` and `MaterialIds.silicon`; and a test-local structure whose one film layer names `{ materialId = MaterialIds.glass152; version = VersionNumber.first.next }` over a lower half-space at `MaterialVersionId.firstOf MaterialIds.glass152` answers both versions, while its `referencedMaterials` is `MaterialIds.glass152` alone. The fact `referencedMaterials covers films, repeated cells, the substrate plate, and the lower half-space` (`MaterialProxyTests.fs`) passes unchanged.

**Acceptance.** After the tags land, `EntryLifecycle`, `EntryProtection` and `PinState` MUST each carry `value` and `tryOfDb`, and `referencedMaterials` MUST be the projection of `referencedMaterialVersions`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `lifecycle, protection and pin states round-trip their database tags`, `referencedMaterialVersions keeps every referenced material version, a repeated cell once` and the unchanged `referencedMaterials covers films, repeated cells, the substrate plate, and the lower half-space`; and build, elevation and the nine s08 invariants MUST pass.
